{"name":"Poplar Kitten","hex":"#ece9e9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"poplar","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various deciduous trees of the genus Populus.","Wood from the poplar tree."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/poplar"},{"term":"kitten","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A young cat, especially before sexual maturity (reached at about seven months).","A young rabbit, rat, hedgehog, squirrel, fox, beaver, badger, etc."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To give birth to kittens."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kitten"}],"entries":[{"title":"Poplar kitten","blocks":[{"text":"The poplar kitten is a species of moth in the family Notodontidae. The species was first described by Nikolaus Joseph Brahm in 1787. They are found throughout Europe and in North Africa, Mongolia, Kazakhstan and Xinjiang."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Furcula_bifida01.jpg/330px-Furcula_bifida01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poplar_kitten"},{"title":"Populus","blocks":[{"text":"Populus is a genus of over 60 species of deciduous flowering plants in the family Salicaceae, native to temperate, subarctic, and montane regions of Eurasia, North America, and North Africa, and to the tropical highlands of East Africa. English names variously applied to different species include poplar, aspen, and cottonwood."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Lapo_gyslos.jpeg/330px-Lapo_gyslos.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Populus"},{"title":"Kitten","blocks":[{"text":"A kitten is a juvenile cat. After being born, kittens display primary altriciality and are fully dependent on their mothers for survival. They normally do not open their eyes for seven to ten days. After about two weeks, kittens 